  "slug": "docking-dynamics-049f",
  "summary": "Sequence-based models now extend editing-outcome prediction from DNA base editors to ADAR-mediated RNA editing, including variant effects.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational prediction, from sequence context, of how genome and RNA editing outcomes arise. BEguided provides variant-specific guide design and comparison across 38 base-editor profiles, with BEguidedOFF for off-target prediction. EditFinder is a sequence-based model for A-to-I RNA editing that predicts editing sites and how genetic variants alter editing probability. What is new here is the extension of such prediction to variant-level effects on RNA editing and the systematic comparison across base-editor profiles. A third preprint, on InDel mutational signatures in 887 multiple myeloma whole genomes, is heterogeneous with respect to this thread: it concerns repair-deficiency signatures and treatment outcome rather than editing. All three items are preprints, and the summaries report no head-to-head benchmarks against established tools.",
